{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/569722-optional-rules-for-beast-clade","id":569722,"title":"Optional Rules for Beast: Clade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-26T16:14:21-07:00","id":569722,"title":"Optional Rules for Beast: Clade","content":"Since Beasts are all about the primal, base fears of humanity and family, but they themselves are segregated into families I had an idea. For example an Anakim can be a giant cyclops, a frost giant, etc. Why isn't there sub-orders of beasts that are similar and share traits? Maybe they specifically find a type of kin as well? This is just a messy piece of optional game material, but I call these: Clades!<br /> <br /> The Clades offer 5 new powers that are not quite atavisms or nightmares. These maybe similar as in overlaying the soul with the physical (ie: atavism) or using a nightmaresque ability, or actually have a physical influence on the world via the mental. These are adaptations that come with certain steps. I got two Clades and see what you guys think. Here's one as a sample:<br /> <br /> <br /> Jungle Behemoths<br /> Open to: Anakim and Ugallu<br /> Kin: Changelings (Beast, Elemental), Werewolves, Changing Breeds, Mages (Thyrsus)<br /> Background: These are the beasts that traverse primordial jungles and forests of nightmare to stalk prey.<br /> <br /> Adaptations:<br /> 1. Knowledge of the Green Hell<br /> Prerequisite: Stamina 3, Lair 2<br /> Dice Roll: N/A<br /> Effect: In forested or heavily vegetated areas, the user gets +2 die to a survival roll.<br /> Cost: 0<br /> <br /> 2. Mighty Horns<br /> Prerequisite: Brawl or Weaponry 3, Lair 2<br /> Dice Roll: Brawl or Weaponry 3+ Lair vs Supernatural Tolerance + Stamina<br /> Effect: Ethereal horns appear and strike target.<br /> Cost: 0<br /> <br /> 3. Parting the Green Tide:<br /> Prerequisite: Lair 3, Presence 4,<br /> Dice Roll: N/A<br /> Effect: All vegetation in an area parts for you as Moses did the Red Sea. This applies even in the thickest green vegetation and sharp, thorned thickets. Good to chase down prey.<br /> Cost: 0<br /> <br /> 4. Great Roar of Sundering Might<br /> Prerequisite: Lair 5, Presence: 4<br /> Dice Roll: Presence+Manipulation vs Supernatural Tolerance+Composure or Stamina<br /> Effect: A massive roar is emitted that strikes a foe flat on the ground and either deals damage to them or strikes them with the Shaken condition.<br /> Cost: 1 Satiety<br /> <br /> 5: Giant Strength and Tread<br /> Prerequisite: Lair 7, Strength 5, and Titanic Blow<br /> Dice Roll: N/A<br /> Effect: For the rest of the scene, your strength is doubled and with Titanic Blow, terrain that's hard to navigate because of sharp rocks or multiple obstacles; the terrain becomes flat as a pancake and easy to traverse.<br /> Cost: 1 Satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6109-imposterzilla","user":"imposterzilla","date":". 06-26-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6109-imposterzilla","name":"imposterzilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:33:24-07:00","id":569777,"title":"","content":"I like it, Maybe Clades can be something of a Z-Splat, like Bloodlines, Krewes, or a Leviathan's Evolutions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},